<div class="wrap narrow-page prose legal">
  <p class="small-note">Last updated 1 October 2026</p>

  <h2 id="short">The short version</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>There are no accounts, no adverts and no tracking of individuals on canoepolo.eu. We count page views anonymously, as explained below.</li>
    <li>Visitors get no cookies.</li>
    <li>We only hold personal information that people choose to send us, such as a message or a tournament listing.</li>
    <li>We never sell or share personal information for marketing.</li>
    <li>Message us on <a href="https://wa.me/353876789927" target="_blank" rel="noopener">WhatsApp +353 87 678 9927</a> and we'll show you, correct or delete anything we hold about you.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="who">Who we are</h2>
  <p>canoepolo.eu is run by a small group of volunteers from the canoe polo community to support the sport. We are not a company, charity or registered organisation, and we don't make money from the site. The volunteers who run the site are responsible for how personal information is handled here. Contact us at <a href="https://wa.me/353876789927" target="_blank" rel="noopener">WhatsApp +353 87 678 9927</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="what">What we collect and why</h2>

  <h3>When you visit the site</h3>
  <p>Like every website, our server has to receive your device's IP address to send you a page. We don't keep web server access logs. We do keep simple anonymous statistics to see which pages are useful: for each day, how many times each page was viewed, which website a visitor came from (the site name only), and how many times links to other sites or downloads were clicked. These are plain counts. We don't save IP addresses, browser details, cookies or anything that identifies a person, and we don't count visitors who send a Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control signal. We also record, as a plain daily count, which country each new visitor appears to be in. To do that your IP address is looked up in a country database in memory at the time of your visit, and only the country code is kept. We also count downloads of documents, team schedules and calendar files, and a few actions such as how far people get in the referee quiz. To see where people leave the site, we hold in memory only, for the length of a visit, the first and latest page you viewed, how many pages and for how long, and when the visit ends (after 30 minutes of no activity) we save only anonymous totals such as "one visit entered on this page and left from that page" and forget the rest. To estimate how many different people visited in a day, a scrambled code made from your IP address and browser is held in memory only, with a key that changes every day, and is never saved to disk. If someone tries to log in to the admin area, their IP address is held in memory for up to 15 minutes to block password guessing, then forgotten.</p>

  <h3>When you message us</h3>
  <p>If you message us on WhatsApp, for example to list a tournament, suggest a video or ask a question, we receive your name and phone number (as shown in WhatsApp) and whatever you write. We use it only to reply and to do what you asked. We delete messages when they're no longer needed, and straight away if you ask. The legal basis is our legitimate interest in running the site and answering you.</p>

  <h3>Tournament listings</h3>
  <p>Tournament pages show event details that organisers send us or that have been published elsewhere, with a link to the source. If an organiser gives us a contact name and email address for publication, those appear on the tournament page. We only publish contact details that were given to us for that purpose. If your details appear and you'd like them changed or removed, message us and we'll do it promptly.</p>
  <p>Please don't send us personal information about other people, especially children, unless they have agreed.</p>

  <h3 id="videos">Videos</h3>
  <p>Videos on the Watch page are hosted by YouTube (Google). The preview pictures come from our own server, so YouTube isn't contacted when you open the page. Only when you press play is the YouTube player loaded, using YouTube's privacy-enhanced mode (youtube-nocookie.com). From then on, Google receives information such as your IP address under <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's privacy policy</a>.</p>

  <h3>Things saved in your own browser</h3>
  <p>The tactics board saves your latest board in your browser, and the referee quiz remembers your best score on your device. This uses your browser's local storage. It stays on your device and is never sent to us. Share links from the tactics board contain the play itself in the link and nothing about you. You can clear this at any time in your browser settings.</p>

  <h3>The admin area</h3>
  <p>People who run the site log in to an admin area. Only then is one cookie (<code>cp_session</code>) set, to keep them logged in and protect forms. It's strictly necessary for that purpose, expires after 12 hours, and is never set for ordinary visitors.</p>

  <p><strong>Translation.</strong> The language links at the top of each page are ordinary links to Google Translate. Nothing is sent to Google unless you click one. If you do, Google shows you a machine-translated copy of the page and Google's own <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a> applies to that visit. Translations are automatic and may contain mistakes, so check anything important (dates, times, rules) in the English original.</p>
  <p class="small-note">IP to country data by <a href="https://db-ip.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DB-IP.com</a>, licensed under CC BY 4.0.</p>

  <h2 id="sms">Text updates (ECC 2026)</h2>
  <p>If you sign up for text updates, we collect your mobile number and the teams you pick. We use them only to text you a confirmation code, a message shortly before those teams play, and their results, and to let you stop. The legal basis is your consent, which you give by ticking the box and entering the code, and which you can withdraw at any time by messaging us on WhatsApp (the number is in every text). Texts are sent through Twilio, a US company, which receives your number and the message text to deliver it (transfers rely on the standard contractual clauses in Twilio's terms). We keep a record of the texts we send you (without confirmation codes) so we can check they were delivered. We keep your number and that record only for the tournament and delete it, together with your choices, soon after it ends, or straight away if you stop. We don't use it for anything else and don't share it with anyone else.</p>

  <h2 id="quiz">Referee quiz leaderboard</h2>
  <p>You can play the referee quiz without giving us anything. If you choose to join the leaderboard, you enter a name, club and country and tick a box to say you are 16 or over and happy for them to be shown publicly with your score. The leaderboard is for people aged 16 and over; if you're younger, please play without joining. We use this only to show the leaderboard and keep it fair. We don't ask for an email address, don't save your IP address, and don't use the details for anything else. Anyone can see the leaderboard, so use a first name and initial if you prefer. To have an entry removed, email <a href="https://wa.me/353876789927" target="_blank" rel="noopener">WhatsApp +353 87 678 9927</a> and we'll delete it. Your legal basis for this is your consent, which you can withdraw at any time.</p>

  <h2 id="cookies">Cookies</h2>
  <p>Visitors to canoepolo.eu get no cookies, so there is no cookie banner. See above for the one cookie used by site admins, and for what YouTube does once you press play on a video.</p>

  <h2 id="sharing">Who else is involved</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>DigitalOcean</strong> hosts the website on a server in London, UK. The UK is recognised by the EU as giving adequate protection to personal data.</li>
    <li><strong>WhatsApp (Meta)</strong> carries the messages you send us on WhatsApp, under <a href="https://www.whatsapp.com/legal/privacy-policy-eea" target="_blank" rel="noopener">its own privacy policy</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>YouTube (Google)</strong>, only when you play a video.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We don't share personal information with anyone else unless the law requires it.</p>

  <h2 id="basis">Legal bases</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Anonymous statistics and country counts:</strong> our legitimate interest in understanding how the site is used. No information that identifies a person is stored.</li>
    <li><strong>Leaderboard:</strong> your consent, which you can withdraw at any time by asking us to remove your entry.</li>
    <li><strong>Messages to us and tournament contact details:</strong> our legitimate interest in running the site and answering you, or your request.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Some tournament information comes from the <a href="https://cpt.kayakers.nl/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Kayakers.nl</a> tournament calendar, used with its maintainer's permission. We link to the source on each listing and don't copy organisers' personal contact details from it.</p>

  <h2 id="keep">How long we keep things</h2>
  <p>Tournament listings stay on the site as a record of past events unless the organiser asks us to remove personal details. The site's database is backed up every night and the last 30 backups are kept, so anything we delete disappears from backups within about a month. Messages are deleted when no longer needed.</p>

  <h2 id="rights">Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under data protection law (including the EU and UK GDPR) you can ask us to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>tell you what personal information we hold about you and give you a copy;</li>
    <li>correct it or delete it;</li>
    <li>stop using it, or limit how we use it;</li>
    <li>object to us using it, withdraw a consent you gave, or ask for your information in a portable format.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Message us on <a href="https://wa.me/353876789927" target="_blank" rel="noopener">WhatsApp +353 87 678 9927</a> and we'll respond within a month. If you're unhappy with how we've handled your information, please tell us first so we can put it right. You can also complain to the data protection authority where you live. In Ireland that's the <a href="https://www.dataprotection.ie/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Data Protection Commission</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="children">Children</h2>
  <p>canoepolo.eu is a general information site for the canoe polo community. We don't knowingly collect information from children, and we don't publish children's personal details. Tournament listings should only contain adult organisers' contact details.</p>

  <h2 id="security">Keeping information safe</h2>
  <p>The whole site uses encrypted HTTPS, the admin area is password-protected, and the server only accepts web traffic and secure administrator connections. No system is perfectly secure, which is one more reason we keep as little personal information as possible.</p>

  <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
  <p>If we change how we handle personal information, we'll update this page and the date at the top.</p>
</div>

